Constrants and Decorators in ODOO:
	Constrants : name field (that alreasdy exist)field names on which the checks will be performed .@constrains only support field names, not dotted fields(related fields, Eg:partner_id.city).


	Computed fields are dynamic fields whose value is calculated based on the values of other fields.
	They are defined using the @api.depends decorator.
	Creating a New Module in Odoo:

	decorators: Decorators allow you to change the behavior of a method

				api.onchange: onchange method will be triggered while we change the value of any of the fields specified with the onchange decorator from the form view
				api.depends: The depends decorator is used to specify the compute dependencies for a computing method.
				api.depends_context: The depends_context decorator is used with non-stored “compute” methods to specify the context dependencies for the methods. The arguments passed will be the key in the context's dictionary and the dependencies must be hashable.
				api.autovacuum: method decorator will be invoked by the daily vacuum cron job defined with the model ir.autovacuum.
				api.model: where self is a record set
				api.model_create_multi :  methods that create multiple records from a single dictionary or a list of dictionaries.
				api.returns :  	used with the methods that return instances of the model.
				api.ondelete: method which is to be called on unlinking the records

				@api.one is used when the method operates on a single record.
				@api.multi is used when the method can handle multiple records.
				@api.model is used for methods that don't require records.


				super() is used to call a method in a parent class.
				It is commonly used in overridden methods to extend or customize behavior.

